{
  "title": "Chloride/bicarbonate ratio does not demonstrate incremental DSST prediction across two NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "In 1,290 NHANES 2011\u20132012 adults aged 60+ and 1,505 separately sampled 2013\u20132014 adults, chloride/bicarbonate ratio added to flexible separate chemistry and demographic predictors changed target weighted MSE by -0.014697 score\u00b2 (-0.0088%), with source-refit/target PSU-bootstrap 95% interval [-0.210649, 0.184745]. This does not demonstrate incremental benefit, equivalence, or absence of an acid-base\u2013cognition association.",
